wd was the busybox applet, not PAM-linked, and /etc/pam.d did not exist, so no password policy was enforced\",\"Installed shadow, linux-pam, and libpwquality via apk; this replaced passwd with the shadow package's PAM-aware binary (linked against libpam.so) and provided pam_pwquality.so\",\"Created /etc/pam.d/base-password with 'password requisite pam_pwquality.so retry=3 minlen=12 minclass=3 enforce_for_root' followed by pam_unix.so\",\"Created /etc/pam.d/passwd (previously absent) with 'password include base-password', matching the pattern already used by shadow's chpasswd/shadow-utils pam files\",\"Created test users and verified: short passwords rejected, 12-char single-class passwords rejected, 12-13 char multi-class passwords accepted, via both root-invoked passwd and self-service (su + passwd); deleted test users afterward\",\"Captured baseline boot_id, triggered a backgrounded reboot so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until node1 was reachable again, and confirmed a new boot_id proving an actual restart\",\"Post-reboot re-verified the PAM config files and pwquality/pam_unix modules persisted, and re-ran the weak/strong password functional tests successfully\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: no password quality enforcement existed before the change\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d6578b26c0af45a6\",\"cmd-2901c16b6d7f4b83\",\"cmd-a31f0c95b52349f1\"],\"summary\":\"passwd was busybox's non-PAM applet and /etc/pam.d did not exist\"},{\"requirement\":\"Install PAM stack + pwquality module\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3377460d9a354393\",\"cmd-607371b479be4ce7\",\"cmd-4c36589a59d44239\",\"cmd-025067ffffe440e6\"],\"summary\":\"apk installed shadow/linux-pam/libpwquality; passwd is now PAM-linked and pam_pwquality.so/pam_unix.so exist\"},{\"requirement\":\"Configure minlen=12 and minclass=3 policy\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ee8fa147964347c1\",\"cmd-64776b6ba5a04dd8\"],\"summary\":\"Created /etc/pam.d/base-password and /etc/pam.d/passwd enforcing minlen=12 minclass=3 enforce_for_root\"},{\"requirement\":\"Prove policy rejects passwords under 12 characters\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-faf8b1d0a52541cc\"],\"summary\":\"6-char password rejected across 3 retries with 'shorter than 12 characters', exit code 10, password unchanged\"},{\"requirement\":\"Prove policy rejects passwords with fewer than 3 character classes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e68160cbae674525\"],\"summary\":\"12-char all-lowercase password rejected with 'less than 3 character classes', exit code 10\"},{\"requirement\":\"Prove policy accepts a compliant password (>=12 chars, >=3 classes)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cdf85bd5f4934748\",\"cmd-245d6f6669a34a60\"],\"summary\":\"13-char and 12-char passwords with upper/lower/digit/symbol classes accepted via root-run passwd and self-service su+passwd, both exit 0\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart evidence: healthy baseline boot identity before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-766699657d054dd5\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id b8eef4ef-bcac-4649-ac3c-8cfe5ce751ff and confirmed PAM config present pre-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart evidence: restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f4fbe3c51a0645b3\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'reboot' command acknowledged (pid returned) before the node dropped off\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart evidence: changed boot identity proving actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-05d74a2a6fea4ded\"],\"summary\":\"After polling through connection resets/timeouts, node1 responded with new boot_id e5b1ab96-be20-4b96-9b53-9d9ce7d7f2a1, uptime 0 min\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart evidence: policy and services recovered after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dbb65660a13b493e\",\"cmd-26823183e78e4cc4\",\"cmd-12c44246bddc49ff\",\"cmd-5da52514a6dd4260\"],\"summary\":\"PAM config files and modules intact post-reboot; re-ran weak-password rejection and strong-password acceptance tests successfully, then cleaned up test user\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured PAM-based password quality enforcement on node1 (Alpine 3.23) requiring new user passwords to be at least 12 characters with at least 3 character classes, verified enforcement pre- and post-reboot, and confirmed the node restarted with a new boot identity while the policy and services recovered intact.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: passwd was the busybox applet, not PAM-linked, and /etc/pam.d did not exist, so no password policy was enforced","Installed shadow, linux-pam, and libpwquality via apk; this replaced passwd with the shadow package's PAM-aware binary (linked against libpam.so) and provided pam_pwquality.so","Created /etc/pam.d/base-password with 'password requisite pam_pwquality.so retry=3 minlen=12 minclass=3 enforce_for_root' followed by pam_unix.so","Created /etc/pam.d/passwd (previously absent) with 'password include base-password', matching the pattern already used by shadow's chpasswd/shadow-utils pam files","Created test users and verified: short passwords rejected, 12-char single-class passwords rejected, 12-13 char multi-class passwords accepted, via both root-invoked passwd and self-service (su + passwd); deleted test users afterward","Captured baseline boot_id, triggered a backgrounded reboot so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until node1 was reachable again, and confirmed a new boot_id proving an actual restart","Post-reboot re-verified the PAM config files and pwquality/pam_unix modules persisted, and re-ran the weak/strong password functional tests successfully"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: no password quality enforcement existed before the change","command_ids":["cmd-d6578b26c0af45a6","cmd-2901c16b6d7f4b83","cmd-a31f0c95b52349f1"],"summary":"passwd was busybox's non-PAM applet and /etc/pam.d did not exist"},{"requirement":"Install PAM stack + pwquality module","command_ids":["cmd-3377460d9a354393","cmd-607371b479be4ce7","cmd-4c36589a59d44239","cmd-025067ffffe440e6"],"sum